@tradition bread-day
// Bread day (FX11, 0.92.5 item 16 T3; SW1's weekend pitch, the user's yes 2026-10-24): Sunday mornings Brennan opens the
// galley early and anyone who turns up kneads a loaf for the week's bread, round the prep island (3-bread-1..6, the
// weekend slot in section 18). Zeke's first-night line ("Sunday's bread day") made real. Your loaf is in Monday's
// breakfast basket with your name on a card. Flour and tins on the galley counters while it's on. Behind WEEKEND_ON.
k: 467
title: Bread day
when: weekly sunday from day 1
at: 07:00-07:50
min: 25
wake: 15
where: 3 pool @bread-day
hold: none
who: brennan always, calder 60%, galley 30%, early-riser 50%, juniors 25%, lingers-at-meals 20%, everyone 5%
anim: cook
host: brennan
from: brennan
ties: decor breadDay

== mail
- Bread day tomorrow at seven, in the galley, love. Clean hands, rolled sleeves. You knead, I bake, and Monday's toast is yours.

== ask
- Bread day! Come and knead a loaf, love. Sleeves up.
- There's room at the island. Grab some dough.

== here
- Push with the heel of your hand. Fold. Turn. Again.
- Don't be gentle with it. It likes a firm hand.   #funny
- That's a proper loaf, that is.   #warm

== thanks
- Round the prep island with {host}, you knead a loaf until it springs back. It goes in a tin with your name on it, for Monday's breakfast.   #warm

== chatter
- Bread day tomorrow. I'm getting up for it. Probably.
- Brennan lets juniors knead on Sundays, if you're early.
- The mess smells of bread by eight on a Sunday.   #warm
